 ## Overview
-SA3D is a framework for 3D object segmentation within radiance fields (NeRF, TensoRF, 3D-GS) that leverages the Segment Anything Model (SAM) to generate initial 2D masks from text or point prompts in a single view [S1, S3]. It distinguishes itself by alternating between mask inverse rendering and cross-view self-prompting to iteratively refine the 3D mask until complete object segmentation is achieved, avoiding manual multi-view annotation [S1, S3]. It builds on [2D-Lift-3D Scene Segmentation](11513-2d-lift-3d-scene-segmentation.md) and differs from [Multi-View Semantic Segmentation Strategy](18471-multi-view-semantic-segmentation-strategy.md) by using self-generated cross-view prompts rather than external multi-view labels.
